hetic redox control of nuclear gene expression</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2005</year><volume>56</volume><issue>416</issue><fpage>1491</fpage><lpage>1498</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15863445</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Scheibe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Backhausen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Emmerlich</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Strategies to maintain redox homeostasis during photosynthesis under changing conditions</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2005</year><volume>56</volume><issue>416</issue><fpage>1481</fpage><lpage>1489</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15851411</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Coupe</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmer</surname><given-names>BG</given-names></name><name><surname>Lake</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systemic signaling of environmental cues in <italic>Arabidopsis</italic> leaves</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>329</fpage><lpage>341</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16330523</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Geigenberger</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolbe</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tiessn</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Redox regulation of carbon storage and partitioning in response to light and sugars</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2005</year><volume>56</volume><issue>416</issue><fpage>1469</fpage><lpage>1479</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15863446</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Buchanan</surname><given-names>BB</given-names></name><name><surname>Luan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Redox regulation in the chloroplast thylakoid lumen: a new frontier in photosynthesis research</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2005</year><volume>56</volume><issue>416</issue><fpage>1439</fpage><lpage>1447</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15851415</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Kwon</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Choi</surname><given-names>EY</given-names></name><name><surname>Choi</surname><given-names>YJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Proteomics studies of post-translational modifications in plants</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>1547</fpage><lpage>1551</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16551683</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Mur</surname><given-names>LAJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Tim</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Carver</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>No way to live: The various roles of nitric oxide in plant-pathogen interactions</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>489</fpage><lpage>505</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16377733</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Grun</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindermayr</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sell</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nitric oxide and gene regulation in plants</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>507</fpage><lpage>516</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16396997</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Crawford</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanisms for nitric oxide synthesis in plants</article-title><source>J Exp Bot</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>471</fpage><lpage>478</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16356941</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Delledome</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Polverari</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Murgia</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The functions of nitric oxide-mediated signaling and changes in gene expression during the hypersensitive response</article-title><source>Antioxidants &#x00026; Redox Sig</source><year>2003</year><volume>5</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>41</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Rouhier</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Vlamis-Gardicas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lilling</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characerization of redox properties of poplar glutaredoxin</article-title><source>Antioxidants &#x00026; Redox Sig</source><year>2003</year><volume>5</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>22</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Link</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Redox regulation of chloroplast transcription</article-title>